> Use question-and-answer pairs: quote your question first, then the answer, and keep the quote when resurfacing.

I sent the full instruction to the mastermind:
- slow down;
- resurface earlier answers as condensed cards;
- each card quotes your question, then gives a tight answer;
- keep the quote when an item comes back.

It drafts the wording and tells me which file it belongs in. The edit stays held and goes in with the batch that waits for your restart. I also asked it to answer again, since its last reply came back empty.
